      "metadata": {
        "split_group": "direct_furnisher_correction"
      },
      "narrative": "The consumer sent a direct dispute to the furnisher's published dispute address. The notice identified the credit-card account, the specific overstated balance, the payoff basis, and included a payoff statement. The dispute concerned covered account information. The furnisher investigated and reported results to the consumer, found the balance inaccurate, but did not notify CRAs or provide the corrected balance. The separate CRA reinvestigation branch was otherwise timely and reasonable: the CRA received a valid dispute, notified the furnisher within 5 business days, modified the tradeline, recorded current status, and sent complete results within 5 business days.\n",
      "provenance": "authored",
      "structured_fields": {},
      "title": "Qualifying direct furnisher dispute found inaccurate but not corrected to CRAs"
    },
